  "body": "# Associated User Story\n\nAs a manager, I want a way for a member to manually leave the organization and disappear from the member sheet, and to manually be able to remove them. So that I can manage which individuals are in my organization.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Members can leave the organization, and officers can remove them, so they disappear from the member sheet\n\n**Sunny:** A member clicks \"Leave Organization\" and confirms, or an officer selects a member and clicks \"Remove Member\" and confirms. The person disappears from the member sheet and dashboard, and they can no longer access member features. The other members' data is not affected.\n\n**Rainy:** The removal fails, the person is removed by accident, or a regular member tries to remove someone else. If it fails, the officer or member sees an error and the person stays on the sheet, rather than ending up half-removed. A confirmation prompt appears before anything is removed. A regular member who tries to remove another member (through the interface or by opening the page directly) sees \"access denied,\" and no one is removed.\n\n# Definition of Done\n\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
